skill: "workforce-compliance-tracker"
sections[3]:
  - "# workforce-compliance-tracker\n\nTrack work-authorization expiries and drive the offboarding compliance sequence with evidence at every step. Use when a visa or permit approaches expiry, when any employment ends, or when an audit asks who verified what and when. The offboarding path hands explicitly to the security zeroize-audit flow.\n\nOwner: role-hr-ops-specialist (pod-people, people_ops). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"work-authorization records work-auth.toon (type, expiry, jurisdiction); roster changes; offboarding policy offboarding-policy.toon per jurisdiction; equipment and access registers\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/people/compliance-calendar.toon with T-90/T-60/T-30 alerts; offboarding-checklist.toon per case with evidence[]; handoff envelope to role-security-auditor (zeroize-audit)\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Build the authorization expiry calendar from work-auth.toon; every record without a verified expiry date is a data defect to chase, not a blank to leave.\n2. Emit T-90, T-60 and T-30 alerts per record; each alert names the renewal action owner and the consequence date (the last day work is lawful without renewal).\n3. On a termination notice, instantiate the jurisdiction-specific offboarding checklist from offboarding-policy.toon; steps without policy backing are proposed as gaps, not assumed.\n4. Sequence the access-revocation steps with the access register; each step records what was revoked, by which system evidence, and when.\n5. Trigger the security handoff: if the departing role had production or data access, emit .agents/handoffs/offboarding-zeroize.toon to role-security-auditor for the zeroize-audit flow; final pay sign-off waits for that closure.\n6. Track equipment return with serial numbers; unresolved items block checklist completion.\n7. Compute final-pay obligations per jurisdiction rules with run_command; anything ambiguous goes to ask_question with the jurisdiction named.\n8. Close the checklist only when every step carries evidence; file compliance-calendar.toon and the checklist as the audit record.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nzeroize handoff to role-security-auditor; final-pay inputs to payroll-cycle-ops.\n"
